<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 60,000 tonnes of wheat, 20,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 60,000 tonnes of wheat, 20,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said it had bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 of Canadian wheat, 20,000 of Australian wheat and 20,000 of Australian barley at its weekly tender, all for October shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000	   Dark northern spring</p>
<p> Canada     20,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p> Australia  20,000	   Standard white</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Australia  20,000	   Feed</p>
</text>
